{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:100821","published":"2026-11-20T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-21T17:30:02.007766615Z","related":["CVE-2026-115560","CVE-2026-126714","CVE-2026-127960","CVE-2026-128064","CVE-2026-128090","CVE-2026-129289","CVE-2026-129291","CVE-2026-129292","CVE-2026-129481","CVE-2026-129496","CVE-2026-129501","CVE-2026-129506","CVE-2026-129538","CVE-2026-15353"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-115560","CVE-2026-126714","CVE-2026-127960","CVE-2026-128064","CVE-2026-128090","CVE-2026-129289","CVE-2026-129291","CVE-2026-129292","CVE-2026-129481","CVE-2026-129496","CVE-2026-129501","CVE-2026-129506","CVE-2026-129538","CVE-2026-15353"],"summary":"Critical: php8.4 security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language. PHP attempts to make it easy for developers to write dynamically generated web pages. PHP also offers built-in database integration for several commercial and non-commercial database management systems, so writing a database-enabled webpage with PHP is fairly simple. The most common use of PHP coding is probably as a replacement for CGI scripts.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * php: PHP-CGI out-of-bounds read and write during PATH_INFO correction (CVE-2026-129538)\n  * php: Timezone cache use-after-free can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-129496)\n  * php: Double free during DOM XML serialization) (CVE-2026-129501)\n  * php: PHP-FPM epoll use-after-free can lead to local privilege escalation (CVE-2026-129291)\n  * php: PHP-FPM request smuggling through an unread HTTP request body) (CVE-2026-129289)\n  * php: PHP-FPM status endpoint XSS via unescaped user and script fields) (CVE-2026-129292)\n  * php: PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm downgrade (CVE-2026-128090)\n  * php: SOAP information disclosure through malformed array dimensions) (CVE-2026-15353)\n  * php: SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity references (CVE-2026-129506)\n  * php: Partially overwritten session files can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-126714)\n  * php: Session serializer mismatch can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-115560)\n  * php: Use-after-free after interrupted session shutdown (CVE-2026-129481)\n  * php: Mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data in plaintext (CVE-2026-128064)\n  * php: Denial of service through folded HTTP response headers (CVE-2026-127960)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * php8.4: Rebase PHP to 8.4.28 in 10.3.z (JIRA:RHEL-310446)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"php8.4","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/php8.4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.4.28-1.el10_3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:100821.json"}},{"package":{"name":"php8.4-bcmath","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/php8.4-bcmath"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.4.28-1.el10_3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:100821.json"}},{"package":{"name":"php8.4-cli","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/php8.4-cli"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.4.28-1.el10_3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:100821.json"}},{"package":{"name":"php8.4-common","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/php8.4-common"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.4.28-1.el10_3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:100821.json"}},{"package"